.TH "CSSUNPARSEDVALUE.CSSUNPARSEDVALUE" "3JS" "August 15, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSUnparsedValue.CSSUnparsedValue \- CSSUnparsedValue:
CSSUnparsedValue() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSUnparsedValue()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSUnparsedValue\f[R] object, which represents a property value
that can\(cqt be parsed into a more specific type \(em typically the
value of a custom property.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSUnparsedValue(members)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]members\f[R]
An array whose values must be either a string or a
\f[CR]CSSVariableReferenceValue\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] value = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnparsedValue([\(dq4deg\(dq]);
\f[B]const\f[R] values = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnparsedValue([\(dq1em\(dq, \(dq#445566\(dq, \(dq\-45px\(dq]);

console.log(value); \f[I]// CSSUnparsedValue {0: \(dq4deg\(dq, length: 1}\f[R]
console.log(values); \f[I]// CSSUnparsedValue {0: \(dq1em\(dq, 1: \(dq#445566\(dq, 2: \(dq\-45px\(dq, length: 3}\f[R]
.EE
.SS \f[CR]CSSUnparsedValue\f[R] with a variable reference
A member can also be a \f[CR]CSSVariableReferenceValue\f[R],
representing a \f[CR]var()\f[R] reference embedded in the value.
This example builds a \f[CR]CSSUnparsedValue\f[R] for a declaration
equivalent to \f[CR]10px var(\-\-bar, blue)\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] fallback = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnparsedValue([\(dqblue\(dq]);
\f[B]const\f[R] varRef = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSVariableReferenceValue(\(dq\-\-bar\(dq, fallback);

\f[B]const\f[R] value = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnparsedValue([\(dq10px \(dq, varRef]);

console.log(value.length); \f[I]// 2\f[R]
console.log(value[0]); \f[I]// \(dq10px \(dq\f[R]
console.log(value[1].variable); \f[I]// \(dq\-\-bar\(dq\f[R]
console.log(value[1].fallback[0]); \f[I]// \(dqblue\(dq\f[R]
.EE
